1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:01,378
Meet SnapFloat.

2
00:00:01,428 --> 00:00:04,309
Screenshots that float, then disappear.

3
00:00:04,359 --> 00:00:06,263
For Linux and Windows.

4
00:00:06,900 --> 00:00:10,052
Press Print Screen, and select what you
want to share.

5
00:00:10,700 --> 00:00:14,503
The screenshot floats in the corner,
already on your clipboard.

6
00:00:15,133 --> 00:00:17,903
Drag it straight into any chat or email.

7
00:00:17,953 --> 00:00:18,907
That's it.

8
00:00:19,533 --> 00:00:21,668
Click the thumbnail to mark it up.

9
00:00:21,718 --> 00:00:25,845
Hide private info finds phone numbers,
emails and one-time codes.

10
00:00:25,895 --> 00:00:29,037
Click any you want to keep, then press
Enter.

11
00:00:29,767 --> 00:00:34,556
Add arrows, numbered steps, and text, on
as many lines as you like.

12
00:00:35,567 --> 00:00:37,696
Select a mark to move or resize it.

13
00:00:37,746 --> 00:00:42,917
Zoom in on a detail with the magnifier, or
pick any colour from the screenshot.

14
00:00:43,633 --> 00:00:45,693
Need the words, not the picture?

15
00:00:45,743 --> 00:00:48,893
Drag over any part, and copy just that
text.

16
00:00:49,533 --> 00:00:50,483
Got a QR code?

17
00:00:50,533 --> 00:00:53,354
Right-click, and the link is copied.

18
00:00:54,133 --> 00:00:56,630
For long pages, use Scrolling capture.

19
00:00:56,680 --> 00:01:00,315
Drag over the part that scrolls, scroll,
and press Add.

20
00:01:00,365 --> 00:01:03,765
SnapFloat stitches it into one tall
screenshot.

21
00:01:04,400 --> 00:01:05,723
Need to show it moving?

22
00:01:05,773 --> 00:01:09,544
Record your screen, and the video floats
in the corner too.

23
00:01:10,567 --> 00:01:15,310
Keep a screenshot on top of your windows
while you work, with Float on screen.

24
00:01:16,167 --> 00:01:19,679
Beautify gives it a clean background,
ready to post.

25
00:01:20,300 --> 00:01:20,979
Took a few?

26
00:01:21,029 --> 00:01:25,850
Combine them into one image, or hold Shift
and drag them all at once.

27
00:01:26,500 --> 00:01:27,758
Closed one too early?

28
00:01:27,808 --> 00:01:31,110
It's still there, under Recent, in the
tray menu.

29
00:01:31,733 --> 00:01:34,579
To catch a menu, use a delayed capture.

30
00:01:34,629 --> 00:01:35,544
Done with it?

31
00:01:35,594 --> 00:01:37,255
Just flick it away.

32
00:01:39,333 --> 00:01:42,900
On Windows, click any window to capture
just that window.

33
00:01:42,950 --> 00:01:45,801
Install it with one click, or with Scoop.

34
00:01:47,700 --> 00:01:53,012
Pick the corner, the timing, the size,
your shortcuts, and the languages to read.

35
00:01:53,633 --> 00:01:56,173
SnapFloat is free and open source.

36
00:01:56,223 --> 00:01:57,767
Get it on GitHub.

